    <briefdescription>
<para>Byte ring of variable-size event records, used by <ref refid="group__baton__node" kindref="compound">Node</ref>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Layout rules: <itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>A record is a 16-byte header (<ref refid="structbaton__record" kindref="compound">baton_record</ref>, serialized byte by byte) followed by the data, padded to a multiple of 4 bytes. </para>
</listitem>
<listitem><para>A record is never split at the end of the buffer. If it does not fit at the end, a SKIP marker is written there (when a header fits) and the record goes to offset 0. A reader that reaches an offset without room for a header, or a SKIP marker, continues at 0. </para>
</listitem>
<listitem><para>head == tail means empty; the producer resets both to 0 when the queue is empty, so the wrapped state never starts from a stale head. </para>
</listitem>
<listitem><para>Records are released only from the head.</para>
</listitem>
</itemizedlist>
The producer (<ref refid="group__baton__node_1ga3c8e0d35c10578eecc4089d0c979d9db" kindref="member">baton_node_send()</ref>) may run in an interrupt; it calls <ref refid="group__baton__queue_1gaa41bcb2dcf676fb81c0342f2dae8f9a2" kindref="member">baton_queue_alloc</ref> with the critical section held and publishes a record by setting <ref refid="group__baton__queue_1gaabe2eb8ef81cc13554d8428b675ef47d" kindref="member">BATON_REC_VALID</ref> last. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
